-- title:
--   Exact mass of a first accepted word after $k$ rejections
-- statement:
--   For a finite Boolean prefix $h$ and $t\in\mathbb N$, write $\mathbb P_{h,t}(E)$ for the fraction of the $2^t$ Boolean suffixes $b$ of length $t$ for which $E$ holds on the tape $h\mathbin{+\!+}b$, extended by zeros beyond its end.
--
--   Write $W_{w,c}(\omega)$ for the natural number obtained by reading $w$ bits of a Boolean tape $\omega$ starting at cursor $c$, most significant bit first, with initial accumulator zero. Let $h$ be a finite prefix and let $t,w,v,k,a\in\mathbb N$ satisfy $w>0$, $v\le2^w$, $a<v$, and $(k+1)w\le t$. Then
--
--   $$\mathbb P_{h,t}\left(W_{w,|h|+kw}=a\land\forall j<k,\ W_{w,|h|+jw}\ge v\right)
--   =\frac{(2^w-v)^k}{2^{(k+1)w}}.$$
--
--   The event specifies $k$ rejected words followed by the particular accepted value $a$. The rest of the suffix is unrestricted.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/BoundedUniformSuccessWords.lean#L168-L261

